Author: CusDeb OS Team
Description: Mizu: Add high-DPI start button and glyph images and scale the other true-size parts.
 The start button, scroll bar arrows, combo box, spin and split button
 arrows, tree view expanders, toolbar chevrons, size grips and radio
 buttons only had 96 DPI images, which were stretched at a higher DPI.
 Add images drawn for 120, 144 and 192 DPI and select them with
 ImageSelectType = Dpi. They are rendered by tools/render_artwork.py and
 tools/render_theme_glyphs.py into CDEX_ARTWORK_DIR; mizu.rc is rebuilt
 when they change. Check boxes get a 20 pixel image for 144 DPI, between
 the theme's 16 and 25 pixel ones.
 .
 The scroll bar button names no glyph images: the theme's two are empty,
 and without them its background image is selected by DPI.
 .
 True-size parts and image glyphs without TrueSizeScalingType were drawn
 at their 96 DPI size at any DPI. Set TrueSizeScalingType = Dpi in those
 sections, so uxtheme scales them. That covers the parts without DPI
 images (MDI buttons, the tooltip close button, explorer bar buttons,
 task band scroll arrows, the taskbar and tray chevrons) and, for the
 parts above, a DPI between two of their images.
Last-Modified: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 19:29:05 +0300

